cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the project and its underlying NASA and Carbon Mapper sources when using these findings."
title: "Methane Map: a reproducible, bounded investigation of public EMIT methane observations"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-19
authors:
  - family-names: Binz
    given-names: Maximilian
repository-code: "https://github.com/MaxiBinz/methane-map"
url: "https://github.com/MaxiBinz/methane-map"
abstract: >-
  An AI-assisted investigation of twenty NASA EMIT V002 methane enhancement
  scenes in the northern Delaware Basin. Fourteen screening components received
  initial assessments: six documented-observation neighborhood associations and
  eight ambiguous responses. The conservative baseline failed its planned
  two-positive-scene recovery gate, and no new methane source was established.
keywords:
  - methane
  - remote sensing
  - EMIT
  - reproducible research
  - research integrity
